1
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,780
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,560
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:40,400
Hey, Bash.

4
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:47,520
Now everything that brought
you and Rem together is gone.

5
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:50,562
Is that your excuse for killing?

6
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:53,977
Haven't you learned anything
over the past hundred years?

7
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:57,657
You can't even regenerate the
scars they carved into your body.

8
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:01,337
It's symbolic of your foolish
waste of energy on this garbage.

9
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:04,437
And it's not your right to
decide whether they live or die.

10
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:05,840
They deserve a chance!

11
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:10,957
What's the use in growing up if the only
thing that grows is your sentimentalism?

12
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:14,100
You're still a
good-for-nothing pathetic whip!

13
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,360
What is that?

14
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:38,060
This is what we're capable of.

15
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:42,140
It's time to take this garbage
and get rid of it forever!

16
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,220
Are you made of me again?

17
00:02:58,060 --> 00:03:00,700
Are you actually aiming at me again?

18
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,020
Eriks? Eriks?

19
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:15,040
How long are you planning
on staying in bed, Eriks?

20
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:17,700
Come on now, get up! Eriks?

21
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,117
Come on, you gotta let us on this bus.

22
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:44,280
You might try and take
this town. I have money.

23
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:48,813
Let me on this bus while we're standing
here arguing it could be too late.

24
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:52,177
You need a ticket to ride,
mister, and I don't give a go.

25
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:53,397
What's the matter with you?

26
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:54,557
Don't you get it yet?

27
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:57,052
Just leave your price, I'll pay anything.

28
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:09,237
There sure seems to be an awful
lot of tension in this town.

29
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,732
Haven't seen you before.

30
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,520
I take it you just arrived. That's right.

31
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:18,434
Well, you have my sympathy because
you're never going to leave this town.

32
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:22,431
What happened over there?

33
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:26,117
This town has been completely
taken over by bandits.

34
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,780
And to make matters worse,

35
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:31,757
they say that crazy fella Vash
the Stampede is running the show.

36
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:34,457
The sheriff went out to
negotiate with the varmints,

37
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,597
but when he came back, he had
doubled his weight in lead.

38
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:41,477
Walking into this town is like
walking into a giant spider's web.

39
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:43,619
The legendary gunman's behind this?

40
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:44,837
What do you think?

41
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,797
Do you believe it?

42
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,237
I don't know what to think.

43
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,897
He is the man who turned
two of the seven cities into

44
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:53,117
ashes and was called mankind's
first localized disaster.

45
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:56,200
Some folks say he put that
huge crater in the moon.

46
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:58,777
I guess you'd have to
be nuts to believe that.

47
00:04:58,860 --> 00:04:59,690
Anyway,

48
00:04:59,773 --> 00:05:01,297
whether the legend is true or not,

49
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:04,617
the one thing I do know is this
town is in some big trouble.

50
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,994
By the way, friend, what is that thing?

51
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:08,720
I'm a traveling priest.

52
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,511
Well, that's good timing.

53
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,294
You'll be useful here.

54
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:15,357
Don't need anything formal, just
some help with the funerals.

55
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,793
They took out the chaplain a while back.

56
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:25,977
What's the big idea you guys?

57
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:27,480
Oh, it's only Lena.

58
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,817
You know what's the big hurry?

59
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:35,277
Was wondering if you
could hide me somewhere?

60
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,917
What'd you do this time?

61
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,900
She doesn't know when to quit.

62
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:41,570
Fun.

63
00:05:41,653 --> 00:05:42,483
That's all the guys.

64
00:05:42,566 --> 00:05:43,396
A pedophile.

65
00:05:43,479 --> 00:05:44,309
He deserved a good thump.

66
00:05:44,392 --> 00:05:45,222
Not really.

67
00:05:45,305 --> 00:05:46,824
All he did was grab a rear end.

68
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,985
Will you keep your mouth shut?

69
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,652
What are you telling me?

70
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,760
Oh, my dear.

71
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,697
Yeah, I'm afraid so, and they
weren't real happy about it,

72
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,917
but at least I don't think
they saw me come in here.

73
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,880
Hey, that's not funny, kid.

74
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:01,968
If what she says is true...

75
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,520
Hey, I wasn't done eating yet.

76
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:14,790
All right!

77
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,357
Where's a little girl who
struck my face with her heel?

78
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,322
She's got a price to pay
and I'm here to collect!

79
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:22,997
That heel looks more
like a whole footprint.

80
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:23,910
Quiet, you!

81
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,611
I can see why he's upset.

82
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,859
It does ruin his boyish good looks.

83
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:30,393
This guy says he saw her enter that bar!

84
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,577
If he's wrong, he's dead!

85
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:32,490
Why?

86
00:06:32,573 --> 00:06:35,237
Because I like to kill scum
who waste my precious time!

87
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:40,261
In any event, this problem will be settled
in approximately three miniscule seconds!

88
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,580
Three, two, one, he dies!

89
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,020
Eriks, wait a second!

90
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,717
What do you think you're doing?

91
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,840
Oh, hey, hi there, Mr. Bandit Man.

92
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,757
We're sorry you didn't find it that funny.

93
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:01,337
I just wanted to say that she's
only a little 12-year-old.

94
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,596
Come on now, have a heart, won't you?

95
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:12,540
Send out the kid now or else!

96
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:14,517
I'm afraid that's not an option.

97
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,617
Looks like you want to kill her
or cause her some kind of harm.

98
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,700
I won't even ask for a free favor.

99
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:21,433
How about if I do this?

100
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,765
Will you let her off the hook?

101
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:27,290
Eriks?

102
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,917
Sorry, but that's not
good enough, blondie.

103
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,217
If you're gonna go down on all fours,
the least you can do is act like a dog?

104
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,237
and I expect some real commitment.

105
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,438
Naturally, that means getting naked.

106
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:46,290
All right.

107
00:07:46,373 --> 00:07:47,203
It's a deal.

108
00:07:47,286 --> 00:07:48,386
You've got to keep your word.

109
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:53,400
I can't let you do this,
Eriks! Please stop!

110
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,677
You don't have to do it!

111
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:55,590
Eriks!

112
00:07:58,500 --> 00:07:59,330
Eriks...

113
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,620
Oh, my God.

114
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,297
It's not your fault, kid.

115
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:12,417
He's got his reasons.

116
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:15,277
We've gotta trust that
he knows what he's doing.

117
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,190
But why?

118
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:18,149
That's just the way he is.

119
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:28,137
I'm gonna thank you for the canine tricks!

120
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:30,573
I've decided to give you a nice big tip!

121
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:38,580
Let's go!

122
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:46,610
Shoot him!

123
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,430
Eriks!

124
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:55,345
Oh, what happened to this man?

125
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,800
He's been shot!

126
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,837
You gotta help him! Eriks again.

127
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,297
What's happened this time?

128
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,617
I can't tell if the bull
is still inside him, Doc.

129
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:06,937
If you had to choose between your life and
your pride, what do you think you'd do?

130
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:10,797
I don't know, but I would never
strip butt naked and bark like a dog.

131
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:13,762
Talent like that comes
easy for a wimp like Eric.

132
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:18,136
If there weren't for that
wimp, you two would be dead!

133
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:20,790
Eric's!

134
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:23,360
My poor Eric's.

135
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:24,817
It's all right, Grandma.

136
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:27,197
They were able to get the
bullet out of him safely.

137
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,809
I'll never understand him.

138
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:30,017
He's one lucky devil.

139
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:33,057
I don't know who this
legendary gunman thinks he is,

140
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:35,197
but what in the hell gives him the right?

141
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:38,162
to steal what precious
little family I have left?

142
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:41,100
Damn him, anyway!

143
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,040
Hey, hey, easy there.

144
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:44,417
Now don't go doing that.

145
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:47,657
You won't last two seconds
against him, don't you understand?

146
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,140
Oh, let me go!

147
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,029
All right, how about
you going to my place?

148
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:54,330
See?

149
00:09:54,413 --> 00:09:56,977
You're all a bunch of cowards,
You weak young whippersnappers.

150
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:58,477
Have no right to order me around!

151
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,797
You're gonna get yourself
killed, you stupid old bat!

152
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:01,777
Oh, shut your mouth.

153
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:03,517
Grandma, don't say that.

154
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,757
I can't, Lina.

155
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,657
All of this is my fault.

156
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:09,037
If I had just stayed away
from them, he wouldn't have.

157
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,560
He wouldn't have.

158
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:12,497
I'm so sorry, Eric.

159
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:15,457
If you're quite finished here, could
you please keep the noise down?

160
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:16,697
There are other patients here.

161
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:18,317
Please forgive me, doctor.

162
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:20,297
I understand how you feel.

163
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:21,837
You don't need to worry.

164
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:24,457
I'll have Eric's move
to the ward right away.

165
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,020
Thank you, Doctor.

166
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:29,431
Lena, let's fetch him a change of clothes.

167
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,390
Okay.

168
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:36,447
Let's move him and get
this place cleaned up.

169
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:37,370
Oh, hello.

170
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:38,837
Sorry I didn't see you there.

171
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,357
He'll be all right now, I assure you.

172
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,852
I know that, no problem.

173
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,647
I just stopped by to
see if I could help out.

174
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,760
You just gonna sleep?

175
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:49,700
Snap out of it!

176
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:51,777
What the hell are you doing to him?

177
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:55,420
He needed it! Doctor! Look
at that! Oh my gosh! Hey!

178
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:00,580
What an amazing recovery.

179
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:03,217
You've regained consciousness so quickly.

180
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:06,557
Excuse me, Doctor, but could you
leave the room for a little while?

181
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,875
Well, yes, I suppose.

182
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:11,147
Don't let him strain
himself, you understand?

183
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:21,340
Well, it's been a long
time, Vash the Stampede.

184
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:37,640
I finally found you, you dumb jerk.

185
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,117
What's a legendary guy like
you doing in a place like this?

186
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,017
You have no idea what I've been through.

187
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:47,197
I could have destroyed this entire
planet with that angel arm of mine.

188
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,280
It gets worse.

189
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:49,957
There's a loss of memory.

190
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,687
I don't remember what I did.

191
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:55,420
That may be true, but you
do know you did it, right?

192
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,097
Oh yeah, I know.

193
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:01,780
I have fragmented visions,

194
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:06,572
but more than anything, there's an ache
in my heart that tells me I did it.

195
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:13,497
I know I'm the one who put
the hole in the fifth moon.

196
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:14,420
It was me.

197
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:22,417
Okay so you did this terrible
thing now what are you so

198
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:26,737
afraid of what you can do you're
living an easy retirement no

199
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:30,397
it's just that i want to live
quietly for once so i decided

200
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:36,217
to change my name and my way of
life why are you here wolfwood

201
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:39,597
what brings you to this town
are you hanging it around for

202
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:44,417
a good laugh actually i came to
take you away away where well

203
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:46,877
if you're asking me for a final
destination i have absolutely

204
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:51,800
no idea however the one thing
i do know is i need your help

205
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:56,680
i spent a lot of time combing
through augusta trying to find you

206
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:05,937
does the name frank marlin happen to ring
a bell all i did was mention your name

207
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:10,837
and he fix the gun for free maybe why give

208
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:13,820
it to me huh i thought you might need it

209
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:24,020
what i need what i want is to
live my life here with them

210
00:13:27,660 --> 00:13:32,437
why was he hospitalized the last
time lena he tried to stop a

211
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:36,344
violent drunk at at the bar and
ended up getting punched himself.

212
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:38,557
And what about the time before that?

213
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:39,980
He fell off at Thomas.

214
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:45,040
Oh, be sure you remember to thank him.

215
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:47,960
I know, I'll remember, Grandma.

216
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:56,160
Hello there, are you okay?

217
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:05,380
You're in horrible shape you poor thing.

218
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:08,700
You must have been through
an awful lot. It's okay.

219
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:09,998
You'll be safe here

220
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,240
Don't worry.

221
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,108
We'll take good care of you

222
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,887
So you're staying here, huh?

223
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:28,257
Whenever I do anything
people die, all right.

224
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:33,857
If you want this pathetic
little existence so bad

225
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:38,597
that you'd give up everything
else then go for it.

226
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:45,457
By the way are

227
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:46,370
you familiar

228
00:14:46,453 --> 00:14:47,457
with the town called Carcasses?

229
00:14:47,540 --> 00:14:50,540
It's a tiny town on the

230
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,297
southern Cornelia region.

231
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:55,262
Something really strange
happened there about six

232
00:14:55,460 --> 00:14:56,290
months ago.

233
00:14:56,373 --> 00:14:59,824
Seems the entire population suddenly
disappeared without a trace.

234
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:03,197
There was no sign of even
the slightest struggle.

235
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,717
Everything in town looked

236
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:08,597
completely normal except that all the
people had vanished like a mirage.

237
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:09,510
They

238
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:13,537
sent in the cavalry and searched the
place over but didn't find a soul.

239
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:14,450
One

240
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:18,017
cavalryman did discover
something very odd though.

241
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:22,477
There was a man's name, painted on the
monument in the middle of the town square.

242
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:26,260
It was one word, carefully written in red,

243
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:28,610
Knives.

244
00:15:35,620 --> 00:15:37,120
Damn you, Knives.

245
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:45,149
It doesn't seem to
matter how far I travel.

246
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:48,257
My destiny is always followed
by blood and gun smoke.

247
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:50,560
The result is the same every time.

248
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,925
Mountains of death and debris.

249
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,717
You've got to come with us, Rem!

250
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,957
Please don't leave us!

251
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,569
Dash, take care of nerves!

252
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,340
No, Rem!

253
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:04,520
Come back!

254
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:11,790
What?

255
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:14,160
What should I do?

256
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:15,690
Your gun!

257
00:16:15,773 --> 00:16:16,603
Give me your gun!

258
00:16:16,686 --> 00:16:17,516
Hurry!

259
00:16:17,599 --> 00:16:18,429
Grandma Cheryl, what?

260
00:16:18,512 --> 00:16:19,342
What is it?

261
00:16:19,425 --> 00:16:20,255
It's Lena!

262
00:16:20,338 --> 00:16:21,168
They got her! What? How?

263
00:16:21,251 --> 00:16:22,760
Just give it to me, now! Stop!

264
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,537
You'll throw your life away!

265
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,137
Besides, they've probably
already killed her!

266
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,050
Shut up!

267
00:16:27,133 --> 00:16:27,963
Don't argue with me!

268
00:16:28,046 --> 00:16:28,876
Just give me the gun!

269
00:16:28,959 --> 00:16:29,789
Cheryl, Cheryl, wait!

270
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:06,320
You know, I was kind of
fond of my new life here.

271
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,653
I really hate to leave.

272
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:11,231
Sorry, them's the brakes.

273
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:13,137
Someone's got to get tough around here or

274
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:15,867
those maniacs are going
to destroy this town.

275
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:18,079
They're both gone!

276
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:19,877
Please don't follow us.

277
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,477
Tell everyone to stay where they are.

278
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,913
We've gone to get Lena.

279
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:24,250
By themselves?

280
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:29,538
How many are there?

281
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:31,020
About 200.

282
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:33,400
100 for each of us, huh? Yep.

283
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:35,855
Well, that's not exactly fair to them.

284
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:41,597
Hey, I don't want you
killing anyone, alright?

285
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:43,697
Why don't you just ask me not to breathe?

286
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:45,097
Thou shalt not kill, remember?

287
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:47,600
What kind of church man are you anyway?

288
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:51,615
Whoa, deja vu, I've heard that before.

289
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,882
Now you're starting to
sound like you ain't so...

290
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:02,330
Eric!

291
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,680
Time to kill!

292
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,940
Showtime!

293
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:49,997
Why did I have to go and talk
to someone this filthy anyway?

294
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:51,256
What was I thinking?

295
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:52,820
I guess I must be crazy.

296
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,360
What a mess.

297
00:18:59,580 --> 00:19:03,797
How the hell did those two manage to take
care of all them thugs by themselves?

298
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,240
I have no idea.

299
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,440
I've never seen anyone
so horrifyingly strong.

300
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:14,885
So your mind is made up, then?

301
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,360
Yes, I'm sorry.

302
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:18,820
It's time I go.

303
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,946
Even though I hate to
do this to you and Lina.

304
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,117
Isn't there anything we can do, Eriks?

305
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:27,376
Maybe if you'd tell me about
it, I could help somehow.

306
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:29,140
Thank you, but I can't.

307
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:33,297
Because you see, if I did, I'd only
be putting you and Lina in danger.

308
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:34,615
Here you have a home.

309
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:38,197
You could end up alone again
with no one there to help.

310
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:41,280
That's what worries us the
most about your leaving.

311
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:43,910
I'm sorry.

312
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:48,600
Who would have guessed that
Eriks was Vash the Stampede?

313
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:49,710
Unbelievable.

314
00:19:49,793 --> 00:19:51,220
Yeah, tell me about it.

315
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:55,949
And to think that all this time we were
convinced that this pig man was Vash.

316
00:19:56,320 --> 00:20:00,320
So, you think the legendary gunman's
gonna stick around these parts?

317
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:02,060
Shoot, don't even go there.

318
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:03,577
Haven't we suffered enough?

319
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:06,060
Yeah, we oughta run him out right now.

320
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,480
She cried, huh?

321
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:20,090
That's a shame.

322
00:20:20,173 --> 00:20:21,003
I didn't know.

323
00:20:21,086 --> 00:20:21,916
Gee, no, I feel bad.

324
00:20:21,999 --> 00:20:24,957
I guess maybe I was acting
just a little bit too pushy.

325
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,687
You don't need to apologize.

326
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,030
Mr.

327
00:20:28,113 --> 00:20:30,320
Preacher, please take good care of Eriks.

328
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:35,380
Unlike you, he's a bumbling fool of a
goody-goody and a sweet, gentle soul.

329
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:38,177
Lena and I have always
known somewhere deep

330
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:40,657
in our hearts it was too good to be true.

331
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:43,657
We knew Eriks would probably
have to leave us someday.

332
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:45,980
Yet we chose not to believe it.

333
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:47,060
Bless him.

334
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:51,360
It doesn't change the fact that
we're losing a member of the family.

335
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:52,840
Please, Mr.

336
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,780
Wolfwood, don't forget that.

337
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:57,860
I'm truly sorry.

338
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,060
I really am.

339
00:21:00,180 --> 00:21:01,298
I'm sorry, Grandma.

340
00:21:24,380 --> 00:21:25,460
There.

341
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:26,860
It's all done.

342
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:37,720
Lena.

343
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:45,211
Thank you for everything.

344
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:50,300
I only wanted to keep you safe.

345
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:54,720
But somehow, it turned
out the other way around.

346
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:56,740
I was too weak.

347
00:21:57,860 --> 00:21:59,036
Don't be ridiculous.

348
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,190
Thank you.

349
00:22:03,273 --> 00:22:04,300
I'm sorry.

350
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:06,110
No, Lina.

351
00:22:06,193 --> 00:22:08,160
It's me who should be saying that.

352
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:32,140
Lina, thank you, and goodbye for now.

353
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:50,560
In the blue sky, the
wind is in the future.

354
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:55,160
The light of the day of the sky,

355
00:22:56,260 --> 00:22:57,380
as you can see,

356
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:01,580
as you can see?

357
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,270
Let's go.

358
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:46,597
I'll see you

359
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:49,280
next time.

360
00:24:06,760 --> 00:24:08,840
Strong will can stir the heart,

361
00:24:09,140 --> 00:24:12,493
but a will too strong can cut
off the heart's visibility.

362
00:24:12,820 --> 00:24:16,291
The sorrow of a man bereaved
of his family turns into hate,

363
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:19,675
which eventually metamorphoses
into the intent to kill.

364
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:22,452
The man's finger reaches for the trigger.

365
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:24,420
Sins change people.

366
00:24:24,940 --> 00:24:26,920
Sin begets sin.

367
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:30,217
But I, I still want to believe.

368
00:24:30,300 --> 00:24:34,400
I want to believe in the heart,
the heart that feels the sin.
